package patterncatalyst:cargo-kafka-handler@0.1.0;

/// The ch23 Kafka message HANDLER for the cargo domain, as a WebAssembly
/// component.
///
/// EXPORTS `wasmcloud:messaging/handler@0.2.0` — invoked once per delivered
/// Kafka message — plus `wasmcloud:messaging/types` (the `broker-message`
/// record handler.wit's `use` pulls in), exported explicitly alongside handler
/// per the house convention of always listing a types-only interface a world's
/// functional interfaces depend on.
///
/// IMPORTS the cargo domain's `booking` and `handling` interfaces (+ the
/// pure-type `types`) from the repository contract and, on every message,
/// ensures the cargo is on record (`book-cargo` when `get-cargo` reports none)
/// before calling `register-handling-event`, a write against the same cargo
/// domain Parts 2-5 use. These imports are satisfied two ways: on minikube the
/// native `cargo-kafka-host` consumer composes this component with the cargo
/// provider via `wac plug` (../kafka-host); on OpenShift a wadm `link` trait
/// wires them at deploy time (../openshift/wadm-kafka.yaml), the runtime-link
/// shape from ch20.
///
/// `wasmcloud:messaging@0.2.0` is vendored under wit/deps/messaging (the
/// upstream wasmCloud/messaging WIT package, verbatim). `patterncatalyst:cargo`
/// is a path dependency to the repository contract (Cargo.toml) — the contract
/// stays byte-for-byte pristine; this component defines only its own world.
world cargo-kafka-handler {
    export wasmcloud:messaging/types@0.2.0;
    export wasmcloud:messaging/handler@0.2.0;

    import patterncatalyst:cargo/types@0.1.0;
    import patterncatalyst:cargo/booking@0.1.0;
    import patterncatalyst:cargo/handling@0.1.0;
}
